---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Supply chain manifest · enprot">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-3">Supply chain manifest</h1>
  <p class="text-enprot-muted mb-6">
    Vendor → customer flow: manifest enumerates sources, deps, builder, signatures.
    Distinct from provenance (build-time) — supply-chain manifest is distributable.
  </p>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Scenario</h2>
    <p>
      A vendor distributing software wants to attest to: which sources were used, which
      dependencies (with hashes), which build commands, which tests ran. Customers verify
      the manifest before installing. The manifest travels with the artifact — the customer
      doesn't need access to the vendor's build logs.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Vendor side</h2>
    <pre class="bg-enprot-ink text-enprot-paper p-4 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code>cd my-crate/
enprot scm init
enprot scm add src/
enprot scm add Cargo.toml
enprot scm deps Cargo.toml   # adds each [dependencies] crate hash
enprot scm attest --signer vendor.pem
# publishes manifest.v1.ept alongside the .crate file</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Customer side</h2>
    <pre class="bg-enprot-ink text-enprot-paper p-4 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code>curl -O https://vendor.example/my-crate-1.0.crate
curl -O https://vendor.example/manifest.v1.ept

cat > customer-policy.toml &lt;&lt;EOF
[chain]
trust_roots = ["ed25519:$(enprot fingerprint vendor.pub)"]

[scm]
allowed_licenses = ["MIT", "BSD-2-Clause", "Apache-2.0"]
forbidden_deps = ["openssl-sys"]   # policy: no openssl
EOF

enprot scm verify --policy-file customer-policy.toml manifest.v1.ept</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Differential verification</h2>
    <pre class="bg-enprot-ink text-enprot-paper p-4 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code># What changed between v1 and v2 of the manifest?
enprot scm diff manifest.v1.ept manifest.v2.ept
# Output: added deps, removed deps, changed source hashes, new signers</code></pre>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
      Audit-friendly: a security team can see exactly what changed between releases without
      diffing the entire manifest by hand.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Ecosystem support</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
      <li><strong>Cargo</strong>: parses <code>Cargo.toml</code> <code>[dependencies]</code>; resolves via cargo index</li>
      <li><strong>npm</strong>: parses <code>package.json</code> + <code>package-lock.json</code></li>
      <li><strong>pip</strong>: parses <code>requirements.txt</code> + <code>pyproject.toml</code></li>
      <li>Leverages <code>cargo-deny</code> for license info, <code>cargo-audit</code> for advisories</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Capability framing</h2>
    <p>
      Vendor holds <code>Signer(vendor_fp)</code>; customer holds
      <code>Verifier(vendor_fp)</code> plus a <code>Reader</code> capability if their CAS
      mirror has the dependency blobs. License/dependency policy is enforced locally —
      the customer decides what's acceptable.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Status</h2>
    <p>
      Specified in <a href="https://github.com/engyon/enprot/blob/main/TODO.finalize/31-supply-chain-manifest.md" class="text-enprot-accent hover:underline"><code>TODO.finalize/31</code></a>.
      Depends on Stage 1 + Stage 3 (INCLUDE).
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
